WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:22.356 --> 00:00:23.816
<i>And so it began.</i>


00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.027
<i>Thirty thousand years ago,</i>


00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:29.530
<i>man discovered his best friend-</i>


00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:33.868
Ooh!


00:00:33.951 --> 00:00:35.536
<i>Dogs were man's best friend</i>


00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.875
<i>and only animal companion
for the next 15,000 years.</i>


00:00:42.126 --> 00:00:43.920
<i>And then...</i>


00:00:45.296 --> 00:00:48.049
<i>Cats are in the house,
y'all! Whoop, whoop!</i>


00:00:51.093 --> 00:00:54.430
<i>The next 15, 000 years, cats
and dogs fought each other.</i>


00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:58.434
<i>Hissing and barking and
breaking things along the way.</i>


00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:03.940
<i>With the emergence of technology, harmless
skirmishes grew into diabolical plots</i>


00:01:04.023 --> 00:01:08.945
<i>as cats and dogs tried to eliminate
each other as human companions.</i>


00:01:09.028 --> 00:01:11.364
<i>Eventually, humans grew tired.</i>


00:01:11.447 --> 00:01:13.366
<i>So dogs and cats
had to do something</i>


00:01:13.449 --> 00:01:17.578
<i>if they wanted to stay the number one and
number two animals in the human household.</i>


00:01:17.662 --> 00:01:19.622
<i>Actually, fish are number one-</i>


00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:21.832
<i>Fish don't count.</i>


00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:27.088
<i>Anyway, cat and dog leaders
worked together to stop these plots</i>


00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:31.801
<i>and formed an organization called
the Furry Animals Rivalry Termination.</i>


00:01:31.884 --> 00:01:34.428
<i>Or FART!</i>


00:01:34.512 --> 00:01:37.265
<i>- Ah, it's not really a thing.
- It's totally a thing!</i>


00:01:37.348 --> 00:01:39.433
<i>The purpose of the
Furry Animals Rivalry...</i>


00:01:39.517 --> 00:01:41.519
<i>Ahem. FART.</i>


00:01:41.602 --> 00:01:46.357
<i>Was to monitor potential
plots, feline or canine,</i>


00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:51.153
<i>and stop them before they
interfered with the human world.</i>


00:01:51.237 --> 00:01:55.866
<i>The good news is when we
opened up wide and let loose FART,</i>


00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.995
<i>the most silent and deadly
organization of all time,</i>


00:01:59.078 --> 00:02:02.707
<i>we were able to stop
those plots and many others.</i>


00:02:02.832 --> 00:02:07.878
<i>The last decade has been the most peaceful
one between the two species in centuries.</i>


00:02:07.962 --> 00:02:09.964
<i>Ha, I wouldn't say centuries.</i>


00:02:10.047 --> 00:02:13.009
<i>Well, you would be wrong.</i>


00:02:18.389 --> 00:02:22.435
<i>Ah... Home sweet home.</i>


00:02:31.235 --> 00:02:35.781
<i>That's me, Roger.
As in Roger Federer,</i>


00:02:35.865 --> 00:02:38.951
<i>the best tennis
player of all time.</i>


00:02:39.035 --> 00:02:43.456
<i>That's Max. My human. He used
to practice outdoors, on the court.</i>


00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:46.500
<i>I would fetch tennis balls
for him, but now, well...</i>


00:02:49.795 --> 00:02:52.131
<i>He does... that.</i>


00:02:56.969 --> 00:03:00.473
<i>Hey! That's me, Gwen.
You know, as in Stefani.</i>


00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:06.312
<i>And let me introduce you to my
fabulous person, the one, the only Zoe!</i>


00:03:08.397 --> 00:03:11.442
<i>Mm, she's under there somewhere.</i>


00:03:11.525 --> 00:03:16.530
Driving me crazy!


00:03:25.831 --> 00:03:28.376
<i>Yeah, she's not really
a morning person.</i>


00:03:41.555 --> 00:03:43.432
- Morning, honey.
- Morning, Mom.


00:03:43.516 --> 00:03:46.852
- Did you sleep well?
- Yeah, I guess.


00:03:46.936 --> 00:03:50.231
- This will put some pep in your step.
- Hmm.


00:03:50.314 --> 00:03:55.152
- Kale juice, spinach juice, celery juice.
- Yeah.


00:03:58.989 --> 00:03:59.824
Good?


00:03:59.907 --> 00:04:01.325
- Mm-hm.
- Drink up.


00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:03.494
So close, honey.


00:04:03.577 --> 00:04:06.455
State championships
are just around the corner,


00:04:06.539 --> 00:04:10.084
I think we can
win it all this year.


00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:11.168
Mm, mm.


00:04:11.252 --> 00:04:12.503
Yeah, for sure.


00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:14.964
Mm-hm.


00:04:15.047 --> 00:04:18.300
<i>And they think drinking
out of a toilet is gross.</i>


00:04:18.384 --> 00:04:22.054
Listen, I got an alert this
morning about your workout.


00:04:22.138 --> 00:04:24.515
I noticed your foot work
was a little slow today.


00:04:24.598 --> 00:04:26.605
I get alerts when you
miss your target numbers.


00:04:26.617 --> 00:04:28.018
What else do you get updates on?


00:04:28.102 --> 00:04:30.479
Your heart rate. How much
time you spend in the bathroom.


00:04:30.563 --> 00:04:32.332
Your heart rate when
you're in the bathroom.


00:04:32.344 --> 00:04:33.041
Boundaries, Mom!


00:04:33.065 --> 00:04:34.733
Just saying. So you
want some more?


00:04:34.817 --> 00:04:36.902
- I know you like it.
- Hmm.


00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.250
- Morning, Zoe-Zoe.
- Good morning.


00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:55.463
- Um, let me make you breakfast.
- It's okay. I got it.


00:04:55.546 --> 00:04:56.922
I'll heat up burritos.


00:04:57.006 --> 00:04:59.163
<i>You're probably
thinking, "Gwen, you're</i>


00:04:59.175 --> 00:05:01.677
<i>nothing but a pampered,
sheltered house cat."</i>


00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.220
<i>And you'd be right.</i>


00:05:03.304 --> 00:05:07.433
No way. You can heat those up?


00:05:07.516 --> 00:05:09.185
No wonder mine are
always so crunchy.


00:05:09.268 --> 00:05:13.481
<i>But one day, we're gonna go outside
and have great adventures together.</i>


00:05:13.564 --> 00:05:15.024
<i>Don't worry. I'll protect her.</i>


00:05:15.107 --> 00:05:16.442
<i>I'm like a ninja.</i>


00:05:19.111 --> 00:05:20.529
<i>I'm okay!</i>


00:05:20.613 --> 00:05:23.657
- How was the gig last night?
- Uh...


00:05:23.741 --> 00:05:24.783
It fell through.


00:05:24.867 --> 00:05:29.955
But I stayed in the coffee shop
and a new song came to me.


00:05:30.039 --> 00:05:31.373
Like a gift from above.


00:05:31.457 --> 00:05:35.211
- That's great, Dad. Let's hear it.
- Yeah. Yeah. It's like, uh...


00:05:43.469 --> 00:05:47.181
♪ <i>Run, run, run I
gotta get away ♪</i>


00:05:47.264 --> 00:05:51.143
♪ <i>Run, run, run Something,
something, something</i> ♪


00:05:51.227 --> 00:05:53.187
♪ <i>Run, run, run</i> ♪


00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:54.772
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.


00:05:54.855 --> 00:05:57.900
See, the thing is, I wrote the lyrics
out on a napkin and then I forgot,


00:05:57.983 --> 00:06:00.319
and then I blew my nose
and then I put in my pocket.


00:06:00.402 --> 00:06:03.197
And then it was just a
mushy, snotty, gooey nothing.


00:06:04.657 --> 00:06:08.744
- Okay. It will come back to you.
- Yeah.


00:06:08.827 --> 00:06:10.246
Yeah.


00:06:10.329 --> 00:06:13.832
Don't forget, Dad, a million
people bought your first album.


00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:15.417
Twenty years ago.


00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.562
Eddie Vedder says you're
the grungiest guy in grunge.


00:06:17.586 --> 00:06:20.172
Eddie Vedder.


00:06:20.256 --> 00:06:23.008
Ah! Hot! You got
asbestos fingers?


00:06:23.092 --> 00:06:24.927
Hot. Hot. Hot. How
do you do that?


00:06:27.555 --> 00:06:31.267
Mm. That tastes so much better!


00:06:32.268 --> 00:06:34.645
Dad, don't give up, promise?


00:06:35.854 --> 00:06:37.231
I promise.


00:06:43.028 --> 00:06:44.363
Bye, Gwen. Have a good day.


00:06:46.407 --> 00:06:48.993
- Bye. Love you.
- Bye. Love you.


00:07:09.138 --> 00:07:12.850
<i>♪ Obstacles are only rocks for the
calm And it's a race against the clock ♪</i>


00:07:12.933 --> 00:07:14.602
♪ <i>And you've got
the perfect timin</i>' ♪


00:07:14.685 --> 00:07:17.062
<i>♪ Bring the thunder So we
all can catch the lightning ♪</i>


00:07:17.146 --> 00:07:19.177
♪ <i>The only thing that
cuts diamond is diamond</i> ♪


00:07:19.189 --> 00:07:19.898
Hold that door!


00:07:19.982 --> 00:07:25.821
<i>♪ I've been waiting all my
life Just for this one night... ♪</i>


00:07:25.904 --> 00:07:27.072
Thank you.


00:07:29.408 --> 00:07:30.993
I'm sorry. Did you
say something?


00:07:31.076 --> 00:07:33.704
Whatever, dude. You do you.


00:07:35.664 --> 00:07:39.376
<i>♪ I've got the heart of a
champion And I will... ♪</i>


00:08:15.329 --> 00:08:20.000
As you may have guessed,
we are not your average pets.


00:08:23.295 --> 00:08:27.424
We're two of the baddest, most
kick-butt FART agents you've ever seen.


00:08:27.508 --> 00:08:30.719
Actually, we're just risk
assessment analysts.


00:08:30.803 --> 00:08:33.055
- <i>Please say the password.</i>
- Beethoven.


00:08:33.138 --> 00:08:34.682
<i>Incorrect.</i>


00:08:34.765 --> 00:08:36.558
- Uh, Rin Tin Tin.
<i>- Wrong.</i>


00:08:36.642 --> 00:08:38.394
- Air Bud.
<i>- Not even close.</i>


00:08:38.477 --> 00:08:39.311
- Snoopy?
<i>- Negative.</i>


00:08:39.395 --> 00:08:40.604
- Old Yeller?
<i>- Incorrect.</i>


00:08:40.688 --> 00:08:43.023
- Scooby-Doo?
- Uh, Garfield.


00:08:43.107 --> 00:08:46.568
<i>- You got it, sister.</i>
- Seriously?


00:08:46.652 --> 00:08:47.695
I put in a request.


00:08:54.827 --> 00:08:56.787
How was the night shift, Old Ed?


00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.825
Well, back's a
little stiff. I've been


00:08:58.837 --> 00:09:01.166
meaning to order one
of those standing desks.


00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:02.960
I meant with the monitoring.


00:09:03.043 --> 00:09:06.672
Well, mostly I've been just watching
these bubbles float across the screen.


00:09:08.173 --> 00:09:10.217
Hey, Ed, that's a screen saver.


00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.886
Oh, you and your
fancy high-tech gadgets.


00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:16.223
In my day, we had to trust
our instincts and communicate.


00:09:16.306 --> 00:09:18.100
And we were out
there on the streets.


00:09:18.183 --> 00:09:22.938
Oh, I wish they'd send us out in
the field. I'm dying to see some action.


00:09:23.021 --> 00:09:25.315
- We're just monitors.
- Pfft.


00:09:25.399 --> 00:09:28.068
Yeah. And how boring is that?


00:09:28.152 --> 00:09:31.655
It's like I always
say, "Boring is good."


00:09:31.739 --> 00:09:32.948
Not.


00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:45.002
Ah, roast beef.


00:09:45.085 --> 00:09:46.587
I'm not gonna even ask.


00:09:49.173 --> 00:09:52.217
- Catch you kids on the flippity-flop.
- Stellar effort, Ed.


00:09:55.763 --> 00:10:01.935
Monitors 44871 and 44872,
logging in for Zone 867.


00:10:02.019 --> 00:10:04.833
<i>The FART system is
functioning flawlessly.</i>


00:10:04.845 --> 00:10:07.941
<i>And the worldwide
threat level remains at low.</i>


00:10:08.025 --> 00:10:10.194
Copy that, chief. Great news.


00:10:10.277 --> 00:10:12.988
Yeah. If you like
rotting away at a desk.


00:10:13.071 --> 00:10:17.367
<i>Uploading your links now.
Carry on, monitors. HQ out.</i>


00:10:23.081 --> 00:10:26.168
Really? What is it
with dogs and trees?


00:10:26.251 --> 00:10:29.588
Very complex. Your
kind would never grasp it.


00:10:29.671 --> 00:10:32.174
Ah. Yes. Yes, you're
absolutely right.


00:10:32.257 --> 00:10:34.718
How could we possibly understand
such a sophisticated ritual?


00:10:34.802 --> 00:10:36.720
Hold the phone.


00:10:36.804 --> 00:10:38.597
I got a canine near
the animal hospital.


00:10:42.309 --> 00:10:45.187
Oh, I bet he's
planning something.


00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:48.190
- Just a stray.
- Looks suspicious to me.


00:10:48.273 --> 00:10:50.692
Could be a serious plot
against feline patients.


00:10:52.402 --> 00:10:54.488
Not the diaper. Not the diaper!


00:10:54.571 --> 00:10:56.323
And... the diaper.


00:10:58.158 --> 00:10:59.493
Oh, I'm gonna be sick.


00:10:59.576 --> 00:11:02.663
Let me guess, too complex
for my kind to grasp?


00:11:02.746 --> 00:11:05.040
Nope. That's just disgusting.


00:11:06.291 --> 00:11:10.754
Nothing exciting ever happens
anymore. You guys had all the fun.


00:11:10.838 --> 00:11:12.589
Take it from someone who knows,


00:11:12.673 --> 00:11:16.718
there was nothing fun about
those major plots back in the day.


00:11:16.802 --> 00:11:21.223
A lot of good agents, both dog
and cat, got injured or worse.


00:11:21.306 --> 00:11:24.560
- Wait, you saw some action?
- Enough to know it wasn't for me.


00:11:24.643 --> 00:11:29.606
At least you were out there. Hey,
you ever give anyone the old...?


00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.485
What the feline is that?


00:11:35.362 --> 00:11:37.155
Initiate reboot protocol.


00:11:37.239 --> 00:11:38.448
Initiating.


00:11:38.532 --> 00:11:40.576
Probably a power failure.


00:11:40.659 --> 00:11:43.453
<i>In case you're wondering,
this is not a power failure.</i>


00:11:43.537 --> 00:11:46.665
<i>But "failure" is the
perfect word to describe</i>


00:11:46.748 --> 00:11:50.961
<i>what's just happened to your
elaborate monitoring system.</i>


00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:53.881
<i>I shut down all communications
from your headquarters</i>


00:11:53.964 --> 00:11:56.800
<i>to every other station
in your network.</i>


00:11:56.884 --> 00:11:59.928
<i>Just try and control
your FART now!</i>


00:12:00.012 --> 00:12:01.638
Told you that was a thing.


00:12:01.722 --> 00:12:03.348
What's going on?
Who's doing this?


00:12:03.432 --> 00:12:08.478
<i>I am the most nefarious
villain the world has ever seen!</i>


00:12:13.233 --> 00:12:15.652
- Is that it? Is he done?
- This is not good.


00:12:15.736 --> 00:12:18.229
Honestly, I thought the
laugh was kind of weak.


00:12:18.241 --> 00:12:20.532
I'm thinking needy
with self-esteem issues.


00:12:20.616 --> 00:12:22.910
Probably a chihuahua or smaller.


00:12:22.993 --> 00:12:24.536
<i>I'm still here.</i>


00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.872
<i>I accidentally hit
the mute button.</i>


00:12:26.955 --> 00:12:29.602
<i>Just know that as
you sit there helplessly</i>


00:12:29.614 --> 00:12:32.336
<i>in your secret bunkers
all over the planet,</i>


00:12:32.419 --> 00:12:37.883
<i>my brilliant plan is already sending
the world of dogs and cats into chaos.</i>


00:12:37.966 --> 00:12:40.010
Chaos? What kind of chaos?


00:12:44.473 --> 00:12:47.811
This is madness. You
won't get away with it.


00:12:47.823 --> 00:12:49.061
<i>I already have.</i>


00:12:52.814 --> 00:12:56.068
We've gotta do something. You
canines designed this system.


00:12:56.151 --> 00:12:58.195
Tell me you butt-sniffers
have a backup plan.


00:12:58.278 --> 00:13:02.449
Uh... Oh, dear
God. We're doomed.


00:13:07.204 --> 00:13:09.206
- That's it, honey!
- Let's go, Max.


00:13:10.624 --> 00:13:13.168
That's it, kiddo.
Follow through.


00:13:13.251 --> 00:13:15.087
Force him to use your backhand.


00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:16.880
Forehand, Max. Forehand.


00:13:20.676 --> 00:13:21.969
Nice swing.


00:13:22.052 --> 00:13:23.720
Good.


00:13:23.804 --> 00:13:25.347
Power shot. Power shot.


00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:28.141
All eyes will be on the state
tennis tournament next week,


00:13:28.225 --> 00:13:30.268
as the boys gun for
the championship.


00:13:30.352 --> 00:13:34.731
<i>Led by local phenom, Max Harper.</i>


00:13:34.815 --> 00:13:37.484
Max will try to complete an
undefeated regular season


00:13:37.567 --> 00:13:38.986
against Central High tomorrow,


00:13:39.069 --> 00:13:42.280
as a tune-up before
the state championship.


00:13:42.364 --> 00:13:44.574
Follow through. Pull
over your shoulder.


00:13:44.658 --> 00:13:49.371
Susan. You know how I feel about you
coaching during practice. I'm the coach.


00:13:49.454 --> 00:13:50.706
I've got the hat.


00:13:50.789 --> 00:13:53.125
You ordered that
hat off the Internet.


00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:55.627
I'm gonna have to
ask for the whistle too.


00:13:56.962 --> 00:13:59.256
I'm keeping the hat.


00:14:13.145 --> 00:14:14.145
Hey, honey.


00:14:20.777 --> 00:14:23.196
The biggest problem with
FART, besides the obvious,


00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:24.865
is that it was designed by dogs.


00:14:24.948 --> 00:14:29.536
We never would have needed FART if you
cats weren't always plotting and scheming


00:14:29.619 --> 00:14:32.122
and trying to disrupt
nature's intentions.


00:14:32.205 --> 00:14:33.749
"Nature's intentions"?


00:14:33.832 --> 00:14:38.295
Three words, hair ball.
Man's best friend, period.


00:14:38.378 --> 00:14:40.380
That's four words. Cat nap!


00:14:46.803 --> 00:14:47.803
Where were we?


00:15:02.027 --> 00:15:04.988
Whoa, what is it?


00:15:19.211 --> 00:15:21.588
What are you doing? That
thing may be about to blow.


00:15:23.298 --> 00:15:24.674
What did you do that for?


00:15:24.758 --> 00:15:26.760
- Sorry. Couldn't help myself.
<i>- Hello? Hello?</i>


00:15:26.843 --> 00:15:28.637
<i>- Pick up the phone. Is anyone there?</i>
- Wait.


00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.555
- It's talking.
<i>- What's the matter with you?</i>


00:15:30.639 --> 00:15:32.849
<i>Answer this phone,
you nincompoops.</i>


00:15:32.933 --> 00:15:34.893
- That sounds like the chief.
<i>- It is the chief.</i>


00:15:34.976 --> 00:15:39.106
Whoa, how about that? It's a
phone. High-tech. No buttons.


00:15:39.189 --> 00:15:40.315
<i>We've been hacked.</i>


00:15:40.398 --> 00:15:43.151
<i>Someone has shut
down our online systems.</i>


00:15:43.235 --> 00:15:45.987
<i>This old landline is the only
way we can communicate.</i>


00:15:46.071 --> 00:15:48.949
- Who do you think is responsible?
<i>- We have no idea.</i>


00:15:49.032 --> 00:15:53.495
<i>But a crime like this has Mr. Tinkles
and Kitty Galore written all over it.</i>


00:15:53.578 --> 00:15:55.664
Knew it. Always the cats.


00:15:55.747 --> 00:15:58.041
Watch who you're
accusing, mister!


00:15:58.125 --> 00:15:59.292
Or what?


00:15:59.376 --> 00:16:00.376
<i>Stop it, you two!</i>


00:16:00.418 --> 00:16:03.255
<i>It appears they've done
something that increases the hatred</i>


00:16:03.338 --> 00:16:05.715
<i>between cats and
dogs everywhere.</i>


00:16:05.799 --> 00:16:08.507
<i>It's clearly affecting
both of you already.</i>


00:16:08.519 --> 00:16:09.970
Not me. He started it.


00:16:10.053 --> 00:16:11.388
- Did not.
- Did too!


00:16:11.471 --> 00:16:14.266
<i>Enough! Hit the big red button.</i>


00:16:26.945 --> 00:16:29.865
<i>Open it and eat one
now. Each of you.</i>


00:16:29.948 --> 00:16:34.578
<i>They've been specially modified with
lavender, valerian root and passion flower.</i>


00:16:34.661 --> 00:16:36.037
Hmm.


00:16:36.121 --> 00:16:38.999
- What do they do?
<i>- They're still in their beta phase.</i>


00:16:39.082 --> 00:16:41.531
<i>But if they work properly,
you should notice</i>


00:16:41.543 --> 00:16:44.171
<i>your disdain for one
another begin to wear off.</i>


00:16:44.254 --> 00:16:48.300
So you want us to be your
test monkeys? After you.


00:16:48.383 --> 00:16:50.135
No. After you.


00:16:50.218 --> 00:16:51.636
No, no, no. Doggies first.


00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:54.014
Oh, no, please. After you.


00:16:54.097 --> 00:16:56.266
- Rock, paper, scissors for it?
- You're on.


00:16:56.349 --> 00:16:58.435
One, two, three.


00:16:58.518 --> 00:17:00.145
- What is that?
- Is that a rock?


00:17:00.228 --> 00:17:01.813
<i>Just do it!</i>


00:17:11.072 --> 00:17:13.867
I owe you an apology.


00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:16.411
Apology accepted.


00:17:16.494 --> 00:17:18.455
Your coat is so soft.


00:17:18.538 --> 00:17:21.124
And your breath smells
like freshly mowed grass.


00:17:21.208 --> 00:17:24.169
<i>We haven't studied
any long-term effects yet.</i>


00:17:24.252 --> 00:17:26.963
<i>But they should keep you
guys from killing each other</i>


00:17:27.047 --> 00:17:29.466
<i>while you solve this case.</i>


00:17:29.549 --> 00:17:31.259
Did you say, "We
solve the case"?


00:17:31.343 --> 00:17:35.764
<i>Yes! We may not know who is
behind this plot, but we do know where.</i>


00:17:35.847 --> 00:17:40.727
<i>Before our computers went down, they were
able to pinpoint the origin of the hack.</i>


00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:42.395
<i>It came from your zone.</i>


00:17:42.479 --> 00:17:46.149
<i>The perpetrator we're looking
for is within a five-block radius</i>


00:17:46.233 --> 00:17:48.318
<i>of where you're
sitting right now!</i>


00:17:48.401 --> 00:17:49.694
Yes! We're on it, chief.


00:17:49.778 --> 00:17:53.073
Wait a second. We're not
field agents, we're just monitors.


00:17:53.156 --> 00:17:56.576
Who are you sending to take
the lead on this? Who's in charge?


00:17:56.660 --> 00:18:00.789
<i>Bottom line, this starts
and ends with you two.</i>


00:18:00.872 --> 00:18:04.459
<i>You'll need to put together a
support team from within your building.</i>


00:18:04.542 --> 00:18:07.003
<i>We cannot trust outsiders.</i>


00:18:07.087 --> 00:18:09.047
From within this building?


00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:11.336
But there are only a few
other cats and dogs that


00:18:11.348 --> 00:18:13.385
live here and none of
them have any training.


00:18:13.468 --> 00:18:16.471
<i>Well, it's up to you
two to get them ready.</i>


00:18:16.554 --> 00:18:20.308
<i>If we don't stop this now, it
could lead to an all-out war</i>


00:18:20.392 --> 00:18:22.269
<i>between cats and dogs.</i>


00:18:22.352 --> 00:18:26.982
<i>The fate of canines and felines
everywhere is in your paws!</i>


00:18:27.065 --> 00:18:28.358
<i>HQ out.</i>


00:18:45.834 --> 00:18:49.546
I thought we were doing okay,
Dad. I mean, with your song royalties.


00:18:49.629 --> 00:18:52.924
Well, we are okay, Zoe,
and we're gonna be okay.


00:18:53.008 --> 00:18:56.511
Just things have been a
little slow lately, that's all.


00:18:56.594 --> 00:19:01.308
I can help. I can get a
job at the mall or babysit.


00:19:01.391 --> 00:19:03.685
No, no, no. This is
not your responsibility.


00:19:04.686 --> 00:19:08.023
The only thing is we may
have to find a smaller place.


00:19:08.106 --> 00:19:11.318
Or a bigger car with
an actual back seat.


00:19:11.401 --> 00:19:13.611
You mean, move? Again?


00:19:13.695 --> 00:19:17.032
Just to save on rent. But same
neighborhood, same school...


00:19:17.115 --> 00:19:18.450
And pets, right?


00:19:18.533 --> 00:19:21.536
I just started looking, Zoe.
We'll do the best we can.


00:19:22.996 --> 00:19:26.833
Hey. We're gonna be fine. Okay?


00:19:29.169 --> 00:19:32.130
Listen, I gotta go
see about a job.


00:19:32.213 --> 00:19:36.718
What kind of job? A studio
musician? Live performance?


00:19:36.801 --> 00:19:38.470
Um, not exactly.


00:19:43.641 --> 00:19:45.018
There's pasta in the fridge.


00:19:45.101 --> 00:19:47.103
I know. I cooked
something. Movie at 7?


00:19:47.187 --> 00:19:48.480
Movie at 7.


00:19:48.563 --> 00:19:51.399
Oh, hey, hey. Don't
forget your guitar.


00:19:53.443 --> 00:19:55.528
- Love you. Bye.
- Love you too. Bye.


00:20:02.035 --> 00:20:07.415
Solving this caper, we're gonna need a
crew. Qualified, dependable specialists.


00:20:07.499 --> 00:20:11.503
A computer expert, one getaway
driver, and a master of disguise.


00:20:11.586 --> 00:20:12.796
Are we robbing a casino?


00:20:12.879 --> 00:20:15.757
This is my first assignment,
okay? Give me this.


00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:20.220
The chief said we can only
use pets from within this building.


00:20:20.303 --> 00:20:25.016
We've got Old Ed, but
besides him, not a lot of options.


00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:27.727
- There's Clyde in 6D.
- He wears a diaper!


00:20:27.811 --> 00:20:29.938
He could track someone's
scent from a mile away.


00:20:30.021 --> 00:20:31.356
Doggy diaper. Enough said.


00:20:31.439 --> 00:20:32.440
Um...


00:20:32.524 --> 00:20:34.449
Well, how about Zelda
on the fourth floor?


00:20:34.461 --> 00:20:36.486
Nope. Cross her path,
seven years' bad luck.


00:20:36.569 --> 00:20:40.407
- Um, isn't that a broken mirror?
- You wanna take that chance?


00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:43.118
Lexie in the penthouse?


00:20:43.243 --> 00:20:46.496
What animal allows a human
to dress her? No self-respect.


00:20:46.579 --> 00:20:49.165
Anastasia, Leopold, Maximus?


00:20:49.249 --> 00:20:52.836
Worms, fleas, explosive
diarrhea. And that's just Anastasia.


00:20:54.003 --> 00:20:56.381
Okay. So that just leaves...


00:21:06.558 --> 00:21:08.893
- Duke.
- Looks like we found our muscle.


00:21:08.977 --> 00:21:12.564
Scared to death of that guy, by
the way. Does he even speak?


00:21:12.647 --> 00:21:15.817
No one knows.
So that's our crew?


00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:18.445
You, me, Old Ed and Duke?


00:21:18.528 --> 00:21:23.032
That's right. The greatest
team the world has ever seen.


00:21:23.116 --> 00:21:25.034
Cat nap!


00:21:25.118 --> 00:21:28.371
- Oh, brother.
- Now let's do this!


00:22:18.296 --> 00:22:20.173
<i>Pablo! Pablo!</i>


00:22:20.256 --> 00:22:21.466
<i>Pablo!</i>


00:22:29.432 --> 00:22:33.144
Yes! Thank you. Yes. Thank you.


00:22:33.228 --> 00:22:34.103
Yes.


00:22:34.187 --> 00:22:37.565
Thirty-four cans will
be a new world record.


00:22:37.649 --> 00:22:39.442
Go, Pablo! You can do it.


00:22:39.526 --> 00:22:41.611
Go, Pablo. Go!


00:22:41.694 --> 00:22:42.987
You can do it!


00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:49.661
Yeah! Take to the skies,
boss. Take to the skies!


00:22:51.329 --> 00:22:53.248
Ow!


00:22:56.167 --> 00:22:57.585
Getting closer, boss.


00:23:03.174 --> 00:23:05.426
So, Zeek.


00:23:06.719 --> 00:23:11.432
The head honcho around here
is a parrot who can almost fly?


00:23:11.516 --> 00:23:15.270
Maybe we should nominate
a fish who can almost swim.


00:23:15.353 --> 00:23:19.941
I'm a cockatoo. You're
new to our organization.


00:23:20.024 --> 00:23:24.737
Pets with Out-of-the-Ordinary
Pedigree, or POOP for short.


00:23:24.821 --> 00:23:26.864
So I'll let you
slide this one time.


00:23:26.948 --> 00:23:31.744
The owner clips my wings to
keep me from flying off my perch.


00:23:31.828 --> 00:23:35.665
Tell me, wise guy, you plan
on going to a loving family soon?


00:23:35.748 --> 00:23:38.001
Maybe a kid to
play with, great food,


00:23:38.084 --> 00:23:40.962
- reverse osmosis water.
- Aren't we all?


00:23:41.045 --> 00:23:43.256
Shelly, how long you been here?


00:23:43.339 --> 00:23:46.467
Ah. Fifteen months, <i>sacré bleu.</i>


00:23:46.551 --> 00:23:50.430
- Zeek, how about you?
- Six hundred and twelve days.


00:23:50.513 --> 00:23:52.849
Me, I've been here six years.


00:23:52.932 --> 00:23:55.602
And never once
taken home as a pet.


00:23:55.685 --> 00:23:57.937
In fairness, you guys
live up to a hundred years.


00:23:58.021 --> 00:24:00.148
Who wants to make
that kind of commitment?


00:24:00.231 --> 00:24:01.274
Listen, 10 legs.


00:24:01.357 --> 00:24:08.281
Do you know how many puppies and
kittens have found homes during that time?


00:24:08.364 --> 00:24:09.490
Millions!


00:24:09.574 --> 00:24:12.869
I don't understand. I thought
humans loved all pets.


00:24:12.952 --> 00:24:15.413
Not as much as cats and dogs.


00:24:15.496 --> 00:24:18.374
Which is why they're all at
the front of the store, not us.


00:24:18.458 --> 00:24:22.545
We're stuck back here in the
aisles of chew toys and mice.


00:24:24.213 --> 00:24:27.383
You have no idea
what that's like.


00:24:27.467 --> 00:24:31.387
- Any puppies or kittens?
- No. Just a bunch of weird stuff.


00:24:31.471 --> 00:24:34.682
Funny-looking reptiles
and dopey birds.


00:24:34.766 --> 00:24:37.518
<i>Dopey birds. Dopey birds...</i>


00:24:42.398 --> 00:24:44.400
The secondary pets
never stood a chance.


00:24:44.484 --> 00:24:49.697
Especially after they started their
worldwide peacekeeping organization.


00:24:49.781 --> 00:24:52.200
But as I stood on my
stoop year after year,


00:24:52.283 --> 00:24:54.827
eyeballing the store computer,


00:24:54.911 --> 00:24:59.540
I came up with the idea
of using online piracy


00:24:59.624 --> 00:25:02.418
<i>to hack into their FART system!</i>


00:25:02.502 --> 00:25:05.171
Ooh! Diabolical!


00:25:05.254 --> 00:25:10.134
And my techno-nerd sidekick,
Zeek, developed a frequency


00:25:10.218 --> 00:25:13.888
<i>that makes cats and dogs
even more vicious to each other.</i>


00:25:13.971 --> 00:25:20.937
<i>The signal is being sent now all
over the world via Wi-Fi and cell towers.</i>


00:25:21.020 --> 00:25:26.401
That little phone controls the
fate of cats and dogs everywhere!


00:25:26.484 --> 00:25:31.364
<i>As we speak, cats and dogs
everywhere are at each other's throats,</i>


00:25:31.447 --> 00:25:33.366
<i>creating mayhem and chaos!</i>


00:25:33.449 --> 00:25:37.120
<i>Soon they will be rejected too,</i>


00:25:37.203 --> 00:25:43.167
<i>abandoned by their humans, and they
will feel what it is like to be unwanted.</i>


00:25:43.251 --> 00:25:44.669
To be unloved!


00:26:02.061 --> 00:26:04.313
Not now, Roger.


00:26:06.023 --> 00:26:07.817
Sorry I'm late.


00:26:07.900 --> 00:26:12.029
Roger. Who's a good boy?
Who's a good boy, huh?


00:26:12.113 --> 00:26:13.489
So...


00:26:13.573 --> 00:26:15.658
are you ready for the
big match tomorrow?


00:26:15.742 --> 00:26:17.994
- I guess.
- You guess?


00:26:18.077 --> 00:26:21.873
You've already beat this kid twice.
You shouldn't even break a sweat.


00:26:21.956 --> 00:26:24.167
Uh, hey, after the match,


00:26:24.250 --> 00:26:26.753
some of the boys on the team
wanna go hit the go-kart track.


00:26:26.836 --> 00:26:28.796
- I thought maybe I could too.
- Oh.


00:26:28.880 --> 00:26:32.133
Sweetie, you know
you've got a full schedule.


00:26:32.216 --> 00:26:36.345
Ice bath, massage,
film session, practice.


00:26:36.429 --> 00:26:37.930
Right. It's just...


00:26:40.683 --> 00:26:42.518
Forget I said anything.


00:26:44.812 --> 00:26:46.314
Okay.


00:27:07.543 --> 00:27:10.671
♪ <i>I should've stopped
when I had the chance</i> ♪


00:27:11.964 --> 00:27:15.259
♪ <i>Now I'm in a no man's land</i> ♪


00:27:15.343 --> 00:27:19.597
"No man's land."


00:27:19.680 --> 00:27:24.060
♪ <i>I never, never, never
want to believe it</i> ♪


00:27:24.143 --> 00:27:28.272
♪ <i>I never, never, never
Thought I could leave this ♪</i>


00:27:28.356 --> 00:27:30.149
♪ <i>Run, run</i> ♪


00:27:31.150 --> 00:27:33.736
Do you like that? Yeah?


00:27:35.488 --> 00:27:37.615
- Hey, Zoe-Zoe.
- Hi, Dad.


00:27:37.698 --> 00:27:40.348
Please tell me you're
not selling used cars.


00:27:40.360 --> 00:27:42.328
Customer-service representative.


00:27:42.411 --> 00:27:45.581
Man, I didn't realize how
mean people could be.


00:27:45.665 --> 00:27:48.209
- Try spending a day at my middle school.
- Yeah.


00:27:48.292 --> 00:27:50.419
I know that you own this house.


00:27:50.503 --> 00:27:53.381
We just live here with you.


00:27:54.423 --> 00:27:57.301
Oh. You've been playing?
Working on something?


00:27:57.385 --> 00:28:00.513
- No. Just messing around.
- Oh.


00:28:00.596 --> 00:28:03.516
Cool. Oh, thank you.


00:28:06.686 --> 00:28:08.396
So...


00:28:08.479 --> 00:28:12.191
I found a smaller apartment,
much easier on the wallet.


00:28:12.275 --> 00:28:17.113
But we need to move right away
so we're not paying double rent.


00:28:18.739 --> 00:28:20.032
They take pets, right?


00:28:20.116 --> 00:28:24.704
Listen, I spoke with your Aunt
Lois and she's happy to take Gwen,


00:28:24.787 --> 00:28:27.039
and we can visit her
as often as we want.


00:28:27.123 --> 00:28:29.041
She lives two hours away.


00:28:29.125 --> 00:28:33.379
Zoe, it's not permanent,
you know. It...


00:28:34.380 --> 00:28:35.380
I'll...


00:28:36.215 --> 00:28:37.258
I don't know.


00:28:42.680 --> 00:28:46.392
- Can we sneak her in for sleepovers?
- Absolutely.


00:28:46.475 --> 00:28:48.060
Right?


00:29:02.283 --> 00:29:03.492
Okay, now, listen up.


00:29:03.576 --> 00:29:06.996
Whoever's behind this plot
is somewhere in our zone.


00:29:07.079 --> 00:29:10.833
It's up to us to find
him or her, cat or dog.


00:29:10.917 --> 00:29:16.047
Well, I've been doing this a long time, and
it's always the cats stirring up trouble.


00:29:16.130 --> 00:29:18.633
I say let them clean up
their own mess this time.


00:29:18.716 --> 00:29:20.176
Easy there, gramps.


00:29:20.259 --> 00:29:24.680
It's just as likely that dogs are behind
this, just to make us cats look bad.


00:29:24.764 --> 00:29:26.891
Gramps?


00:29:26.974 --> 00:29:31.520
Yeah. That's what I said. Or
do you need some hearing aids?


00:29:31.604 --> 00:29:33.397
Now, you listen, sassy pants.


00:29:33.481 --> 00:29:36.734
I might be old, but these
paws still know how to fight.


00:29:36.817 --> 00:29:39.111
Would you stop?
There's no time for this.


00:29:41.238 --> 00:29:43.115
Gwen mapped out our zone.


00:29:43.199 --> 00:29:47.119
We know our tech is down,
right? So we gotta go old-school.


00:29:47.203 --> 00:29:50.164
Tomorrow, I say
we hit the streets.


00:29:50.247 --> 00:29:53.459
- It's up to us now.
- Nope. We're analysts.


00:29:53.542 --> 00:29:57.129
We stay right here, in our
building, and we monitor the action.


00:29:57.213 --> 00:30:01.759
We don't participate in it.
Boring is good, remember?


00:30:01.842 --> 00:30:03.761
Well, someone out
there knows something.


00:30:03.844 --> 00:30:06.263
And I am fully confident
this crew can find out,


00:30:06.347 --> 00:30:10.643
this brand-new, how-do-you-do,
out-of-the-blue, cat-and-dog crew.


00:30:11.936 --> 00:30:13.270
Is she okay?


00:30:13.354 --> 00:30:15.022
She's just enthusiastic.


00:30:21.028 --> 00:30:23.447
O, M, to the G.


00:30:23.531 --> 00:30:27.994
This is really
happening. I am outside!


00:30:28.077 --> 00:30:30.621
Yes. Seattle.
Outside, and it's wet.


00:30:30.705 --> 00:30:35.501
It's so much more than I ever
thought it would be. It's so big.


00:30:35.584 --> 00:30:37.610
We're only 20 feet
away from the front door


00:30:37.622 --> 00:30:39.755
of the building. There's
actually a lot more.


00:30:39.839 --> 00:30:42.299
Oh, look at all this space.


00:30:42.383 --> 00:30:44.176
So much space.


00:30:45.928 --> 00:30:50.099
Too much space. Where are all the
walls? Danger! Danger in every direction!


00:30:50.182 --> 00:30:52.518
Gwen, keep it together.
We've got a mission to do.


00:30:52.601 --> 00:30:55.521
- Let's just...
- Animal control, five o'clock!


00:30:56.731 --> 00:30:58.441
Our eye in the sky.


00:30:58.524 --> 00:31:00.568
And it's heading right at you.


00:31:04.113 --> 00:31:05.531
Scramble. Hide.


00:31:05.614 --> 00:31:07.491
Outside bad. Outside bad!


00:31:07.575 --> 00:31:08.993
Whose idea was this?


00:31:17.168 --> 00:31:19.295
No, wait, check that.


00:31:19.378 --> 00:31:21.630
False alarm on the
animal control truck.


00:31:21.714 --> 00:31:24.133
My bad. Just the
ice cream vendor.


00:31:24.216 --> 00:31:28.220
You think you can get me a
Drumstick? I just love those things.


00:31:45.863 --> 00:31:48.113
Before cameras and
monitors and gadgets, we


00:31:48.125 --> 00:31:50.493
got our information
from combing the streets.


00:31:50.576 --> 00:31:57.208
Like in a cop movie. Just gotta find us a
snitch. A pigeon, a weasel, a blabbermouth?


00:31:57.291 --> 00:32:00.628
A cheese eater? Oh, I
think I see one. Cover me.


00:32:05.674 --> 00:32:08.260
Okay, ankle biter,
who's behind the plot?


00:32:08.344 --> 00:32:09.386
Oh, boy.


00:32:09.470 --> 00:32:14.308
I'm onto you, cupcake. And don't think
I'm fooled by the whole toy-group routine.


00:32:15.309 --> 00:32:16.977
Okay, a crafty one.


00:32:17.061 --> 00:32:20.773
Guess I need to dispense
with my good cop.


00:32:20.856 --> 00:32:25.361
Spill the beans, purse
pooch, or you start losing digits!


00:32:27.196 --> 00:32:28.989
Fingers or toe?


00:32:32.576 --> 00:32:33.911
You think it was too much?


00:32:40.793 --> 00:32:44.964
Hey, sarge, FART agent 44871.
What's the word on the street?


00:32:45.047 --> 00:32:46.966
Little small for an agent.


00:32:47.049 --> 00:32:49.677
I'm actually just a
monitor. Long story.


00:32:49.760 --> 00:32:51.262
A lot of domestic calls.


00:32:51.345 --> 00:32:55.558
Mostly cats and dogs mixing it up,
destroying property. You got any leads?


00:32:55.641 --> 00:32:57.685
We narrowed it
down to this zone,


00:32:57.768 --> 00:33:00.646
but the perp took out our
comms, so we're hitting the streets.


00:33:00.729 --> 00:33:02.857
Shaggy dog in the park.


00:33:02.940 --> 00:33:06.902
One of our informants,
always has the 411.


00:33:08.070 --> 00:33:09.196
Tell her Buck sent you.


00:33:10.281 --> 00:33:12.575
Hey, hey, keep it off
the hydrants, buddy.


00:33:13.659 --> 00:33:17.663
Hey, shampoodle, leash it up.
Hey, buddy, where's that collar?


00:33:17.746 --> 00:33:19.832
Consider this a warning.


00:33:22.376 --> 00:33:25.045
Okay, executing covert approach.


00:33:26.463 --> 00:33:28.299
Gotta be cool, not too obvious.


00:33:29.633 --> 00:33:33.762
Whoops! Coming on too strong,
okay, back it up. Reset. Acting normal.


00:33:33.846 --> 00:33:37.266
Okay? Not feeling normal.
What do normal dogs do?


00:33:37.349 --> 00:33:39.143
They sniff trash cans.


00:33:39.226 --> 00:33:41.103
Commence sniffing.


00:33:41.187 --> 00:33:43.272
Ooh. Rotting chili dogs.


00:33:47.318 --> 00:33:48.611
Better get in on this.


00:33:49.653 --> 00:33:52.698
Hey, shaggy, I hear you've
got a poop scoop around here.


00:33:52.781 --> 00:33:54.783
I keep my eyes open.


00:33:54.867 --> 00:33:58.120
Uh, well, you see
anything lately?


00:33:58.204 --> 00:34:02.374
Couple of weeks ago, I heard whispers
that someone was looking to hire a job.


00:34:03.375 --> 00:34:06.212
A hush-hush kind of a job.


00:34:06.295 --> 00:34:08.255
- So who was it?
- I don't know.


00:34:08.339 --> 00:34:12.468
They were right next to me, and
this may come as a bit of a surprise,


00:34:12.551 --> 00:34:15.554
- I didn't see their faces.
- Heh. Imagine that.


00:34:16.805 --> 00:34:21.936
Bottom line, if you need something
done around this town, you go to the cats.


00:34:22.019 --> 00:34:24.855
- The cats?
- The alley cats.


00:34:24.939 --> 00:34:27.775
But they don't come out
till the sun goes down.


00:34:36.951 --> 00:34:41.080
When the world lays eyes
on me, they will cower in terror.


00:34:41.163 --> 00:34:45.292
They didn't think I was worth loving,
so now they will fear me instead!


00:34:48.045 --> 00:34:49.588
Oh, no, no, no.


00:34:49.672 --> 00:34:53.092
Hey, boss, it ain't
working for you.


00:34:53.175 --> 00:34:55.052
Really? I thought
hats were scary.


00:34:55.135 --> 00:34:57.930
Uh, not that one.


00:34:58.013 --> 00:34:59.473
Okay. Okay.


00:34:59.556 --> 00:35:03.644
Prepare to be scared
beyond your imagination!


00:35:12.736 --> 00:35:15.030
No! You don't look scared!


00:35:15.114 --> 00:35:16.657
Of a wizard parrot?


00:35:16.740 --> 00:35:18.158
I'm a wizard cockatoo!


00:35:18.242 --> 00:35:20.536
Oh, well, now I'm scared.


00:35:21.745 --> 00:35:26.458
<i>We are getting reports of global
unrest developing in the pet world</i>


00:35:26.542 --> 00:35:31.088
<i>as canines and felines are suddenly
quarreling at unprecedented levels.</i>


00:35:31.171 --> 00:35:34.591
<i>Take a look at these videos
sent in from our local viewers.</i>


00:35:37.511 --> 00:35:38.721
<i>Wow.</i>


00:35:39.722 --> 00:35:42.850
Glad we're not involved in
any of that mess, right, Gwen?


00:35:42.933 --> 00:35:44.310
You have no idea.


00:35:44.393 --> 00:35:47.730
001493.


00:35:47.813 --> 00:35:50.357
Yeah. A 2 p.m. showing, okay?


00:35:50.441 --> 00:35:52.901
I can confirm you?
All right, thank you.


00:35:52.985 --> 00:35:55.321
Okay, I look forward
to it. Bye-bye.


00:35:56.447 --> 00:35:57.656
How'd it go, champ?


00:35:57.740 --> 00:35:59.074
6-3, 6-3.


00:35:59.158 --> 00:36:02.786
Wow. He put up
quite a fight today.


00:36:02.870 --> 00:36:04.580
Still, a win's a win.


00:36:06.457 --> 00:36:11.670
Yeah. Um... Actually, I lost.


00:36:13.047 --> 00:36:15.424
- You lost?
- That's right.


00:36:15.507 --> 00:36:18.177
Okay. Uh...


00:36:18.260 --> 00:36:21.180
We can just train a
little harder next time.


00:36:21.263 --> 00:36:24.725
We've been taking Sunday mornings <i>off</i>
from practice. Maybe that was a mistake.


00:36:24.808 --> 00:36:28.812
I don't know, Mom, it's...
Maybe I wasn't feeling it today.


00:36:31.023 --> 00:36:35.277
- No fever.
- Good news is, the team actually won.


00:36:35.361 --> 00:36:38.489
The other guys pulled it for
me, so we're still undefeated.


00:36:38.572 --> 00:36:43.619
Oh. Well, that's a
silver lining, I guess.


00:36:46.038 --> 00:36:50.709
<i>Well, it's not uncommon to see behavioral
changes coincide with mating seasons</i>


00:36:50.793 --> 00:36:52.628
<i>or even weather patterns.</i>


00:36:52.711 --> 00:36:55.631
<i>But we've never
seen anything like this.</i>


00:36:55.714 --> 00:36:58.967
<i>Now we're speaking with the
manager of the Paw Street Market,</i>


00:36:59.051 --> 00:37:03.931
<i>who's already seeing this
conflict impacting his business.</i>


00:37:04.014 --> 00:37:05.849
<i>People are skipping
the puppies and kittens</i>


00:37:05.933 --> 00:37:10.521
<i>and taking home reptiles, snakes
and birds, all much easier to care for.</i>


00:37:10.604 --> 00:37:12.147
<i>Well, what about the fish?</i>


00:37:12.231 --> 00:37:13.899
<i>Fish don't count.</i>


00:37:18.487 --> 00:37:21.907
Okay, come clean about your
field-agent days. What happened out there?


00:37:21.990 --> 00:37:24.785
Look, it was a long time
ago. I made a mistake.


00:37:24.868 --> 00:37:27.621
And ever since, I've been
behind a desk where I belong.


00:37:27.704 --> 00:37:29.289
What kind of mistake?


00:37:29.373 --> 00:37:30.499
There was a moment.


00:37:30.582 --> 00:37:33.836
There's always a
moment, and I hesitated.


00:37:33.919 --> 00:37:38.715
My partner, my mentor, got
hurt. I've never gotten over it.


00:37:38.799 --> 00:37:41.357
But listen, we can't
forget that a pet's


00:37:41.369 --> 00:37:44.388
number one job is to
be there for their humans.


00:37:44.471 --> 00:37:46.102
Okay, okay, you're right.


00:37:46.114 --> 00:37:48.851
My boy Max just hasn't
been himself lately.


00:37:48.934 --> 00:37:51.687
I've been trying to help, but he
doesn't have time for me anymore.


00:37:51.770 --> 00:37:55.441
Well, my girl Zoe's been going
through some tough stuff too.


00:37:55.524 --> 00:37:56.524
We might have to move.


00:37:56.567 --> 00:38:01.238
Max sure could use someone to talk to,
preferably someone who could talk back.


00:38:01.321 --> 00:38:03.699
Zoe doesn't have a friend
that understands her, either.


00:38:03.782 --> 00:38:05.909
She just spends most
of her time on her phone.


00:38:05.993 --> 00:38:10.122
Oh, yeah, the phones. Max turns
into a zombie when he stares at his.


00:38:10.205 --> 00:38:13.375
Yeah. Zoe falls asleep with
hers on the pillow right next to her.


00:38:13.459 --> 00:38:16.503
You know, Max used to take me
to play fetch at the park every night.


00:38:16.587 --> 00:38:20.632
Have humans forgotten that their stress
goes down when they engage with their pets?


00:38:20.716 --> 00:38:23.453
These kids don't even
engage with each other.


00:38:23.465 --> 00:38:25.220
Max needs a friend like Zoe.


00:38:25.304 --> 00:38:27.639
Zoe really needs
a friend like Max.


00:38:27.723 --> 00:38:30.100
Meanwhile, a
deranged villain is trying


00:38:30.184 --> 00:38:33.562
to eliminate cats and
dogs as human pets forever.


00:38:33.645 --> 00:38:38.150
And the only lead we have depends
on a shifty collection of vile street cats


00:38:38.233 --> 00:38:40.903
who would trade their
grandmothers for a dead mouse.


00:38:40.986 --> 00:38:43.655
- Why don't you let me talk to them?
- Are you sure you're ready?


00:38:43.739 --> 00:38:46.950
Are you kidding?
I was born ready.


00:38:57.252 --> 00:38:57.700
Shh.


00:38:57.712 --> 00:39:01.465
Sorry. It's a dog thing.
We like to sing along.


00:39:02.925 --> 00:39:04.593
Actually, I changed my mind.


00:39:04.676 --> 00:39:07.721
- I don't wanna do this.
- Rock, paper, scissors?


00:39:07.804 --> 00:39:10.098
- Loser has to face them?
- You're on.


00:39:10.182 --> 00:39:11.892
One, two, three.


00:39:11.975 --> 00:39:14.019
I'm paper. You're rock. I win.


00:39:14.102 --> 00:39:15.541
No, I'm scissors. I win.


00:39:15.553 --> 00:39:18.232
That's not scissors.
How can that be scissors?


00:39:18.315 --> 00:39:19.566
That's totally scissors.


00:39:19.650 --> 00:39:23.111
If you're gonna throw out scissors,
you've gotta grow out those nails.


00:39:26.323 --> 00:39:28.200
Oh.


00:39:29.743 --> 00:39:34.873
Remember, you wanted some action.
This is what you've always wanted.


00:39:34.957 --> 00:39:40.587
Prepare yourself for some disgusting,
frothing mongrels, munching on dead mice.


00:39:40.671 --> 00:39:41.922
Filth upon filth.


00:39:42.005 --> 00:39:43.173
- Psst.
- Oh!


00:39:43.257 --> 00:39:45.634
Over here.


00:39:48.053 --> 00:39:49.053
Elon Musk?


00:39:49.096 --> 00:39:52.140
I'm looking for the alley cats.


00:39:53.267 --> 00:39:55.686
Then it's your lucky day.


00:39:55.769 --> 00:39:57.271
You're an alley cat?


00:39:57.354 --> 00:40:00.023
Why don't you
step into my office?


00:40:00.107 --> 00:40:02.734
You mean, come into the light?


00:40:02.818 --> 00:40:08.574
I thought you guys usually slept outside,
drank out of puddles, ate dead mice.


00:40:08.657 --> 00:40:13.245
We did, until some rich doofus
started parking his Tesla in our alley


00:40:13.328 --> 00:40:15.497
and leaving the windows down.


00:40:15.581 --> 00:40:19.001
Well, I was told by a shaggy dog
that you might have information


00:40:19.084 --> 00:40:21.461
about a job that was
done around here.


00:40:21.545 --> 00:40:24.298
Uh, keep-it-on-the-down-low
kind of job?


00:40:24.381 --> 00:40:26.675
Of course I do.


00:40:26.758 --> 00:40:28.385
I'm the one who did it.


00:40:28.468 --> 00:40:30.637
- You?
- That's right.


00:40:30.721 --> 00:40:34.057
And I was paid
handsomely for it.


00:40:34.141 --> 00:40:35.559
With money?


00:40:35.642 --> 00:40:38.020
No. What would a
cat do with money?


00:40:38.103 --> 00:40:41.231
I got this shiny
ball of tin foil, duh.


00:40:41.315 --> 00:40:44.026
Ooh, ooh, ooh.


00:40:44.109 --> 00:40:45.277
Fine. Ooh.


00:40:45.360 --> 00:40:48.447
- Who hired you?
- Don't know.


00:40:48.530 --> 00:40:54.286
They communicated electronically, sending
text messages about a covert mission.


00:40:54.369 --> 00:40:55.662
So, what was the mission?


00:40:55.746 --> 00:40:59.124
I snuck into the headquarters
of a wireless phone company,


00:40:59.207 --> 00:41:01.585
got some codes
off their computers.


00:41:01.668 --> 00:41:03.253
What kind of codes?


00:41:03.337 --> 00:41:06.632
Wi-Fi and cellular
access codes. Ha-ha.


00:41:06.715 --> 00:41:10.594
Seems like a lot of trouble
just to get some free Internet.


00:41:10.677 --> 00:41:12.054
Ooh. Ha-ha.


00:41:14.973 --> 00:41:17.142
It's just so shiny.


00:41:17.934 --> 00:41:20.354
<i>Oh, it's an epidemic!</i>


00:41:20.437 --> 00:41:24.232
<i>Humans are returning their
cats and dogs by the millions!</i>


00:41:24.316 --> 00:41:27.110
<i>Tell me you've
made some progress.</i>


00:41:27.194 --> 00:41:31.865
Well, we've gathered some intel,
but no idea how the pieces fit yet.


00:41:31.948 --> 00:41:34.993
Well, let's start with
this. What do we know?


00:41:35.077 --> 00:41:39.998
<i>Well, we know some maniac out there
has found a way to ramp up aggression</i>


00:41:40.082 --> 00:41:42.209
<i>between cats and dogs.</i>


00:41:42.292 --> 00:41:46.672
And we know he shut down our entire
system designed to prevent such plots.


00:41:46.755 --> 00:41:49.290
And we know someone
hired the alley cats to


00:41:49.302 --> 00:41:51.968
steal access codes for
Wi-Fi and cell towers.


00:41:52.052 --> 00:41:54.513
One thing has never
made sense to me.


00:41:54.596 --> 00:41:58.934
This plot is devastating
to both cats and dogs.


00:41:59.017 --> 00:42:02.688
What kind of lunatic would
devise a plot that hurts all of us?


00:42:02.771 --> 00:42:08.151
Huh. Hard to read the mind of
a lunatic, especially a cat lunatic.


00:42:08.235 --> 00:42:09.778
Or a dog lunatic.


00:42:09.861 --> 00:42:13.198
Maybe we need to
think outside the box.


00:42:13.281 --> 00:42:15.909
What if it's neither
cat or dog lunatic?


00:42:17.994 --> 00:42:21.665
Who stands to gain from humans
walking away from cats and dogs?


00:42:22.999 --> 00:42:24.376
Other pets.


00:42:24.459 --> 00:42:29.381
So we possibly have a rogue secondary pet
who's bent on pushing cats and dogs aside


00:42:29.464 --> 00:42:30.882
as mankind's favorite.


00:42:30.966 --> 00:42:33.051
<i>Good working theory, agents.</i>


00:42:33.135 --> 00:42:35.429
"Agents." He said agents.


00:42:35.512 --> 00:42:40.851
But how could he possibly be reaching
virtually every cat and dog on the planet?


00:42:40.934 --> 00:42:42.602
Through the food, water?


00:42:42.686 --> 00:42:45.397
Wait. That's it.


00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:47.065
Wi-Fi cell towers.


00:42:47.149 --> 00:42:52.154
He doesn't care about receiving Internet.
He cares about sending frequencies.


00:42:52.237 --> 00:42:58.243
- You mean like heat frequencies?
- That only affect cats and dogs.


00:42:58.326 --> 00:43:00.704
I knew technology was evil.


00:43:00.787 --> 00:43:03.832
<i>Now get to work figuring
out who's behind it.</i>


00:43:03.915 --> 00:43:08.128
<i>We are clearly dealing with a
ferociously frightening criminal.</i>


00:43:12.966 --> 00:43:16.261
♪ <i>Oh, work it Looking,
looking good</i> ♪


00:43:17.512 --> 00:43:19.222
♪ <i>Yes, I'm hot</i> ♪


00:43:19.306 --> 00:43:21.391
♪ <i>I knew I would</i> ♪


00:43:21.475 --> 00:43:22.934
♪ <i>This is fire, baby</i> ♪


00:43:23.018 --> 00:43:25.228
♪ <i>Burn it up, burn
it up You're good ♪</i>


00:43:25.312 --> 00:43:28.774
♪ <i>So good</i> ♪


00:43:29.900 --> 00:43:31.234
♪ <i>Lookin' good, lookin' good</i> ♪


00:43:31.318 --> 00:43:33.111
Oh, none of these
looks are befitting


00:43:33.195 --> 00:43:37.115
the most nefarious villain
the world has ever seen!


00:43:38.283 --> 00:43:42.996
No one is afraid of a cockatoo
in a hat! I need a totally new look.


00:43:43.079 --> 00:43:45.791
A costume that sends
shivers up the spine.


00:43:45.874 --> 00:43:52.464
Sir, it is ready, the costume
you have been waiting for.


00:43:52.547 --> 00:43:56.843
Yes! My robotic
mechanical dog suit!


00:43:56.927 --> 00:44:01.848
Finally, the world will cower when
faced with my slobbering beastliness.


00:44:01.932 --> 00:44:03.725
Reveal it to me.


00:44:03.809 --> 00:44:06.728
Feast your eyes on
my greatest invention.


00:44:10.148 --> 00:44:11.483
It looks so real.


00:44:11.566 --> 00:44:13.610
You wanna take her for a ride?


00:44:13.693 --> 00:44:17.030
Yes. Zip me up inside.


00:44:17.113 --> 00:44:19.491
Time for a test drive.


00:44:21.034 --> 00:44:22.410
Now that I'm outside...


00:44:23.995 --> 00:44:29.417
I must test the full capabilities of this
machine. Let's see. What does this one do?


00:44:32.712 --> 00:44:34.297
Okay.


00:44:34.381 --> 00:44:38.134
What about this
one? And this one?


00:44:38.218 --> 00:44:39.511
This one?


00:44:46.184 --> 00:44:47.602
I just threw up.


00:44:48.770 --> 00:44:49.813
But I swallowed it.


00:45:10.250 --> 00:45:11.751
Some other time, Roger.


00:45:18.008 --> 00:45:22.846
You know, you're just in a little
slump. It happens to everyone.


00:45:22.929 --> 00:45:26.975
We just have to decide
how to get you out of it.


00:45:28.018 --> 00:45:31.688
Maybe a new racket
might help. Huh?


00:45:31.771 --> 00:45:33.481
Something with a bit more power?


00:45:34.482 --> 00:45:36.985
Wow, thanks, Mom.


00:45:37.068 --> 00:45:41.281
We could re-watch the Australian
final between Federer and Nadal.


00:45:41.364 --> 00:45:43.408
That always fires you up, right?


00:45:43.491 --> 00:45:46.494
Hey, Rog, did you like your
breakfast? That's a good boy.


00:45:46.578 --> 00:45:50.081
You know, we could also watch the
video footage of my over-40s club match


00:45:50.165 --> 00:45:51.750
against Sheila Smithers


00:45:51.833 --> 00:45:53.793
when I took her
down in straight sets.


00:45:53.877 --> 00:45:55.879
- She was pregnant.
- Who knew?


00:45:55.962 --> 00:45:57.964
- With triplets.
- Yeah.


00:45:58.882 --> 00:46:01.551
Ha-ha. Listen, Max.


00:46:01.635 --> 00:46:05.138
You know I'm so very proud
of you, right? No matter what.


00:46:05.221 --> 00:46:06.640
I know, Mom.


00:46:07.641 --> 00:46:10.644
- I'll figure it out.
- Okay. Eat up, champ.


00:46:21.404 --> 00:46:24.282
Let me help you
with those, sweetie.


00:46:25.283 --> 00:46:26.368
After I...


00:46:27.202 --> 00:46:28.662
After I take a break.


00:46:28.745 --> 00:46:31.957
Dad, we can't move all of
this stuff to a smaller apartment.


00:46:32.040 --> 00:46:33.625
We need to make choices.


00:46:33.708 --> 00:46:35.418
- You're right.
- Okay. Um...


00:46:38.004 --> 00:46:41.007
- Trash or treasure?
- Treasure. That's my high-school flannel.


00:46:41.091 --> 00:46:42.217
All right.


00:46:42.300 --> 00:46:45.845
Treasure. It's my
college flannel.


00:46:47.222 --> 00:46:50.141
Treasure. It's my
unemployed-starving-artist flannel.


00:46:50.225 --> 00:46:54.354
I think we should treasure the whole box.
We should treasure every moment, actually.


00:46:54.437 --> 00:46:55.897
Label it, "treasure."


00:46:55.981 --> 00:46:57.774
- What else?
- What about these records?


00:46:57.857 --> 00:47:00.694
No. No, no, no. We
can't throw those out.


00:47:00.777 --> 00:47:06.700
Are you kidding me? Neil Young, <i>Live Rust,</i>
that's like a rock 'n' roll holy relic.


00:47:06.783 --> 00:47:07.323
Psst. Psst.


00:47:07.335 --> 00:47:09.244
What else we got here?
Weezer, <i>Green Album,</i>


00:47:09.327 --> 00:47:12.205
reissue, yes, but...
Get over here.


00:47:12.288 --> 00:47:14.332
Ah! You don't have to blind me.


00:47:14.416 --> 00:47:17.157
Oh, here's a
London band, sort of


00:47:17.169 --> 00:47:21.089
little-known. I don't
know, The Rolling Stones.


00:47:21.172 --> 00:47:24.926
Okay, what's the shape of this
album? Octagon. What's that say?


00:47:25.010 --> 00:47:26.845
Stop, that's what it means.


00:47:26.928 --> 00:47:31.599
Gotta keep these. Speaking of
which, where's your record collection?


00:47:31.683 --> 00:47:35.020
- Here.
- Are you crazy? They're both home.


00:47:35.103 --> 00:47:37.605
I think I have a fix.
Meet me in the hall.


00:47:37.689 --> 00:47:41.484
- Oh, and Zoe's phone, hide it.
- What?


00:47:41.568 --> 00:47:46.489
Just do it. We're gonna give our humans
the friends that we can't be right now.


00:48:35.288 --> 00:48:38.958
Hi. Hey, I left my phone upstairs.
Mind if we go back up so I can grab it?


00:48:39.042 --> 00:48:40.376
- Fine.
- Thanks.


00:48:44.756 --> 00:48:47.008
I think I forgot mine too.


00:48:53.098 --> 00:48:54.307
Thirsty?


00:48:56.643 --> 00:49:01.231
Just gotta hydrate. My mom likes me
to get at least 64 ounces before lunch.


00:49:04.025 --> 00:49:05.777
What the...?


00:49:08.238 --> 00:49:12.325
- Hello? Somebody? Can you hear us? Hello!
- Hey! Hey!


00:49:13.868 --> 00:49:14.994
Hello!


00:49:16.162 --> 00:49:17.162
Come on.


00:49:19.124 --> 00:49:21.501
I'm sure it's just
a minute or two.


00:49:24.170 --> 00:49:28.258
What are the chances? We
both forgot our phones today.


00:49:28.341 --> 00:49:30.885
I know. Great.


00:49:39.185 --> 00:49:41.604
I don't even care if I miss
my tennis lesson this morning.


00:49:41.688 --> 00:49:43.064
Really?


00:49:43.148 --> 00:49:45.304
I thought you,
like, ate, drank, and


00:49:45.316 --> 00:49:48.027
breathed tennis with
every inch of your soul.


00:49:48.111 --> 00:49:49.154
Yeah.


00:49:49.237 --> 00:49:50.905
Well, I thought I did too.


00:49:50.989 --> 00:49:54.701
I mean, I even named my
dog Roger, after Federer.


00:49:54.784 --> 00:49:59.122
I don't know. Recently, it's been feeling
more like a job than a hobby, you know.


00:49:59.205 --> 00:50:03.543
- Dude, a bit of unsolicited advice?
- Hit me.


00:50:03.626 --> 00:50:07.005
Chill, chill, and chill.


00:50:07.088 --> 00:50:11.885
- Really? Even that last one?
- Especially that last one.


00:50:15.221 --> 00:50:18.641
So where were you off to
this morning? Guitar lessons?


00:50:18.725 --> 00:50:23.313
Um, no. We're moving tomorrow,
and we're packing boxes.


00:50:23.396 --> 00:50:24.814
I just needed a break.


00:50:24.898 --> 00:50:27.650
You're moving,
like, out of town?


00:50:27.734 --> 00:50:28.985
No.


00:50:29.068 --> 00:50:31.905
We're just downsizing, I guess.


00:50:31.988 --> 00:50:35.450
Same school, new
building, doesn't allow pets.


00:50:35.533 --> 00:50:37.410
You have a cat, right?


00:50:37.493 --> 00:50:40.246
Gwen, as in Stefani.


00:50:40.330 --> 00:50:42.040
Music's kind of our thing.


00:50:42.123 --> 00:50:43.917
Wasn't your dad a musician?


00:50:44.000 --> 00:50:45.460
He is a musician.


00:50:50.924 --> 00:50:52.659
How long do we
leave them in there?


00:50:52.671 --> 00:50:54.844
Until they realize
they're actually friends.


00:50:59.224 --> 00:51:01.768
What? I told you
we like to sing along.


00:51:11.277 --> 00:51:13.905
Notice anything weird
about that ice cream truck?


00:51:13.988 --> 00:51:15.823
Uh, the terrible driving?


00:51:15.907 --> 00:51:17.909
Yeah, and it never
actually stops.


00:51:17.992 --> 00:51:21.329
It's like it's always
there, just watching us.


00:51:22.330 --> 00:51:25.708
I'll go check it out and, uh,
maybe grab a Drumstick.


00:51:31.172 --> 00:51:32.632
Something's not right.


00:51:32.715 --> 00:51:34.092
I've got a bad feeling.


00:51:36.094 --> 00:51:36.928
Whoa!


00:51:37.011 --> 00:51:38.846
- Ed!
- Let go!


00:51:38.930 --> 00:51:40.348
Ed, no!


00:51:40.431 --> 00:51:45.853
That was too easy. Your smartest
agent just walked into my trap.


00:51:45.937 --> 00:51:47.313
Ed!


00:51:49.440 --> 00:51:51.276
Ed! Ed!


00:51:53.778 --> 00:51:58.366
- Good luck finding me now, birdbrains!
- He's been watching us this whole time.


00:51:58.449 --> 00:52:00.410
Just playing with us.


00:52:00.493 --> 00:52:04.414
We're in over our head with this
guy. He's in complete command.


00:52:04.497 --> 00:52:06.249
Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:52:06.332 --> 00:52:08.042
Gas!


00:52:08.126 --> 00:52:10.378
No, wait, brakes!


00:52:11.796 --> 00:52:13.339
Gas.


00:52:13.423 --> 00:52:15.425
Brakes! Brakes!


00:52:15.508 --> 00:52:17.760
Oh, no, a roundabout.


00:52:19.304 --> 00:52:22.598
These things always confuse me.


00:52:22.682 --> 00:52:25.018
Maybe I should take over.


00:52:26.728 --> 00:52:29.022
- Okay, okay.
- Let me help.


00:52:30.023 --> 00:52:32.984
Get back to the
pedals, lizard brain!


00:52:40.992 --> 00:52:42.952
- Anything?
- It's pitch black.


00:52:43.036 --> 00:52:45.339
Wait, I got a flash
on my... phone.


00:52:45.351 --> 00:52:48.791
It's a great effort, but I
think it's time to come...


00:52:48.875 --> 00:52:50.209
Whoa!


00:52:51.210 --> 00:52:52.210
Down.


00:52:52.253 --> 00:52:54.547
- Ow.
- Here, look.


00:52:56.674 --> 00:52:58.301
You okay?


00:52:58.384 --> 00:53:00.845
Yeah, yeah, no, I'm fine, fine.


00:53:22.075 --> 00:53:24.118
Um, zucchini kale bite?


00:53:26.579 --> 00:53:30.083
"No gluten, no dairy, no
soy, no grains, no sugar."


00:53:33.419 --> 00:53:34.419
And no taste.


00:53:43.471 --> 00:53:46.599
- Uh-oh.
- What's uh-oh?


00:53:46.682 --> 00:53:50.937
- Gosh, maybe you're a little too hydrated?
- You can never be too hydrated.


00:53:52.146 --> 00:53:54.273
Unless you're
stuck in an elevator.


00:53:54.357 --> 00:53:56.984
- You have to hold it.
- I don't think I can.


00:53:57.985 --> 00:53:59.445
Now we have a real emergency.


00:54:03.324 --> 00:54:04.492
We lost him.


00:54:04.575 --> 00:54:07.120
Wait. Maybe not.


00:54:24.429 --> 00:54:26.514
Just have to follow the sound.


00:54:36.023 --> 00:54:39.735
- Okay, you gotta distract me.
- Okay. Um...


00:54:39.819 --> 00:54:42.989
- What do you have planned in the summer?
- I'm supposed to go to tennis camp.


00:54:43.072 --> 00:54:45.616
But, you know, recently,
it... What are you doing?


00:54:45.700 --> 00:54:47.535
I'm going whitewater
rafting with my dad.


00:54:47.618 --> 00:54:51.873
I love being out on the water, in the
water... Anything water-related, really.


00:54:51.956 --> 00:54:54.500
- You're not helping.
- Sorry.


00:55:02.550 --> 00:55:04.427
Ooh. Ice cream
truck, six o'clock.


00:55:16.272 --> 00:55:17.648
Ed.


00:55:24.864 --> 00:55:29.243
Ha. I knew you'd find me. Nice
instincts on the howling, by the way.


00:55:29.327 --> 00:55:31.996
- Gotta get you untied.
- There's no time.


00:55:32.079 --> 00:55:33.623
- But...
- And, Roger...


00:55:34.665 --> 00:55:36.375
there will be a moment.


00:55:38.044 --> 00:55:42.924
There's always a moment that you'll
need to make a split-second decision.


00:55:43.007 --> 00:55:47.512
Don't hesitate. Whoever kidnapped
me went inside the pet store.


00:55:48.846 --> 00:55:52.058
Now, get in there
and stop that lowlife.


00:55:56.229 --> 00:55:59.649
Okay, so why are you moving?


00:56:03.069 --> 00:56:05.780
My dad hasn't come out
with a new song in a while.


00:56:05.863 --> 00:56:08.574
He doesn't think he has anything
to say to the younger audience.


00:56:10.785 --> 00:56:12.995
And I had this crazy idea.


00:56:13.079 --> 00:56:16.415
Like, maybe I could write
him one. And revive his career.


00:56:18.751 --> 00:56:21.462
Truthfully, we're not moving.


00:56:22.463 --> 00:56:23.673
We were evicted.


00:56:26.342 --> 00:56:29.595
- I'm sorry. I didn't...
- No, it's fine. I mean...


00:56:29.679 --> 00:56:34.392
I'm here about to pee my pants and I'm
babbling about my stupid tennis stuff...


00:56:34.475 --> 00:56:35.726
It's not stupid.


00:56:37.019 --> 00:56:38.145
I'm glad you did.


00:56:40.565 --> 00:56:43.442
I feel like people assume
things about others. You know?


00:56:43.526 --> 00:56:48.364
For sure. It's like no one
actually really talks anymore.


00:56:50.032 --> 00:56:52.702
It's probably the longest I've
gone without being on my phone.


00:56:53.703 --> 00:56:56.497
It's kind of nice. Isn't it?


00:56:56.581 --> 00:56:58.624
Actually having a conversation.


00:56:58.708 --> 00:57:00.459
Yeah.


00:57:02.086 --> 00:57:04.839
Oh, God. Okay,
you gotta distract me.


00:57:04.922 --> 00:57:07.008
- Let's hear it.
- Hear what?


00:57:07.091 --> 00:57:09.427
The song. The one
you're writing for your dad.


00:57:09.510 --> 00:57:11.053
Absolutely not.


00:57:11.137 --> 00:57:13.135
Do you have something
more important planned


00:57:13.147 --> 00:57:14.974
while we're stuck
here in this elevator?


00:57:15.057 --> 00:57:17.226
No, but it's just...


00:57:17.310 --> 00:57:20.021
Dude, a bit of
unsolicited advice,


00:57:20.104 --> 00:57:22.982
you made me realize I
was overdoing my talents,


00:57:23.065 --> 00:57:25.318
I think you're maybe
underdoing yours.


00:57:34.452 --> 00:57:35.578
This is stupid.


00:57:35.661 --> 00:57:38.289
Come on. You've got this.


00:57:49.592 --> 00:57:52.595
♪ <i>Run, run, run</i> ♪


00:57:53.596 --> 00:57:56.432
♪ <i>Run, run, run</i> ♪


00:58:20.414 --> 00:58:24.126
Ah, like clockwork. Lured
them right into my trap.


00:58:24.210 --> 00:58:26.045
Zeek, clear the store.


00:58:30.091 --> 00:58:33.094
I'm really sorry, everyone. We
gotta leave. Depart the premises.


00:58:33.177 --> 00:58:34.887
Right now, everybody, please.


00:58:34.970 --> 00:58:36.722
- Pete?
- Let's go.


00:58:36.806 --> 00:58:39.642
- Where's my son?
- I'm sorry. I'm sure he's outside.


00:58:41.686 --> 00:58:44.105
What's going
on? Is there a fire?


00:58:44.188 --> 00:58:48.192
It's a diversion. Be
careful. It might be a trap.


00:58:48.275 --> 00:58:50.611
Okay, let's go.


00:58:59.870 --> 00:59:01.205
Come on, you two.


00:59:02.206 --> 00:59:03.791
Right behind you.


00:59:18.973 --> 00:59:22.977
Now, remember, could be
any type of horrible animal.


00:59:23.060 --> 00:59:25.229
Rat, python...


00:59:27.356 --> 00:59:29.150
Or a parrot.


00:59:29.233 --> 00:59:30.609
Aren't you a cockatoo?


00:59:30.693 --> 00:59:32.778
Name's Pablo.


00:59:32.862 --> 00:59:35.322
But you might know me better


00:59:35.406 --> 00:59:39.744
as the most nefarious villain
the world has ever seen.


00:59:47.084 --> 00:59:48.127
You?


00:59:48.210 --> 00:59:49.086
Yes.


00:59:49.170 --> 00:59:50.671
Perhaps you'll remember me.


00:59:50.755 --> 00:59:54.216
After all, I watched you, Roger,


00:59:54.300 --> 00:59:56.719
get adopted from
this very store.


00:59:56.802 --> 00:59:58.012
Not ringing any bells.


00:59:58.095 --> 01:00:00.306
Really? I was in the
cage right across from you.


01:00:00.389 --> 01:00:02.558
- Nope.
- I told you knock-knock jokes on occasion.


01:00:02.641 --> 01:00:04.727
- Still nothing.
- I was right in the cage.


01:00:04.810 --> 01:00:05.728
But why?


01:00:05.811 --> 01:00:09.607
Why wouldn't I? After
all you've done to us.


01:00:09.690 --> 01:00:11.066
What we've done?


01:00:11.150 --> 01:00:13.527
And now it's time to pay.


01:00:13.611 --> 01:00:16.781
Zeek, release our comrades.


01:00:21.202 --> 01:00:22.453
Freedom!


01:00:22.536 --> 01:00:24.121
All right, let's go.


01:00:24.205 --> 01:00:25.831
Let's go.


01:00:33.631 --> 01:00:37.885
Okay, big guy, you're our
enforcer. Time to start enforcing.


01:00:46.727 --> 01:00:50.898
♪ <i>A lovely, fluffy tarantula
Went up the water spout ♪</i>


01:00:50.981 --> 01:00:53.108
♪ <i>Out came the rain and...</i> ♪


01:00:55.569 --> 01:01:00.783
Get that thing away from
me! I'm allergic to spiders!


01:01:00.866 --> 01:01:02.701
Hey, our enforcer speaks.


01:01:02.785 --> 01:01:04.453
Yeah. Bone-chilling.


01:01:04.537 --> 01:01:07.873
With that settled, it's
time to plan your big trip.


01:01:07.957 --> 01:01:09.333
Trip?


01:01:20.261 --> 01:01:22.471
Hey, someone in there?


01:01:22.555 --> 01:01:24.014
Yes, we're stuck.


01:01:24.098 --> 01:01:25.850
- Please help us.
- Please.


01:01:25.933 --> 01:01:29.520
Okay, just give me a minute.


01:01:31.397 --> 01:01:33.190
Finally.


01:01:33.274 --> 01:01:36.277
- Quite the adventure, huh?
- Yeah.


01:01:36.360 --> 01:01:39.363
I'm so glad we finally
got to know each other.


01:01:39.446 --> 01:01:41.866
Yeah, me too.


01:01:41.949 --> 01:01:43.534
Thanks.


01:01:44.994 --> 01:01:45.994
Thank you.


01:02:08.017 --> 01:02:09.184
Uh...


01:02:10.394 --> 01:02:14.106
- I guess he fixed it.
- Yep.


01:02:15.983 --> 01:02:17.109
Uh...


01:02:19.361 --> 01:02:22.114
I better go take Roger out.


01:02:22.197 --> 01:02:24.954
Yeah, you dog people
have to do that, don't you?


01:02:24.966 --> 01:02:25.409
Mm-hm.


01:02:31.665 --> 01:02:35.669
- Can I come?
- Yeah. Yeah, of course.


01:02:41.550 --> 01:02:43.135
Ooh! Sorry about that.


01:02:43.218 --> 01:02:45.971
Roger! Rog!


01:02:46.055 --> 01:02:47.973
I'm home!


01:02:48.974 --> 01:02:50.976
That's strange.
Where could he be?


01:02:51.060 --> 01:02:53.562
- Do you think your mom took him?
- No, she's gone all day.


01:02:54.563 --> 01:02:55.439
Rog!


01:02:55.522 --> 01:02:57.650
- Does he do this a lot?
- Never. I...


01:03:00.736 --> 01:03:02.279
What?


01:03:03.739 --> 01:03:07.743
Oh... Roger has a GPS on
his collar, we can find him.


01:03:11.038 --> 01:03:14.959
- Okay, he's not that far. Come on.
- I gotta drop off my guitar.


01:03:16.502 --> 01:03:19.046
- Stairs.
- Stairs.


01:03:23.175 --> 01:03:26.804
In case you got any
ideas about escaping,


01:03:26.887 --> 01:03:28.847
I think you'll
enjoy island life.


01:03:28.931 --> 01:03:30.391
Island? What island?


01:03:30.474 --> 01:03:33.143
Aldabra island, Indian Ocean.


01:03:33.227 --> 01:03:37.022
Sunshine. Sandy beaches.
Crystal blue waters.


01:03:37.106 --> 01:03:39.066
Mm. Sounds kind of nice.


01:03:39.149 --> 01:03:41.944
And no humans.


01:03:44.697 --> 01:03:47.408
Uh-oh. Hold on. Hold on.


01:03:47.491 --> 01:03:50.494
I don't get it. We've
done nothing to you.


01:03:50.577 --> 01:03:52.871
Oh, but you have.


01:03:52.955 --> 01:03:58.669
While you cats and dogs were keeping
the peace with your worldwide FART system,


01:03:58.752 --> 01:04:02.506
the rest of us pets
sat day after day,


01:04:02.589 --> 01:04:04.133
month after month,


01:04:04.216 --> 01:04:08.137
and in my case, year after year,


01:04:08.220 --> 01:04:11.724
waiting for human
owners that never came.


01:04:11.807 --> 01:04:13.600
That's what this is about?


01:04:13.684 --> 01:04:16.687
That's exactly
what this is about.


01:04:20.190 --> 01:04:21.233
It says he's in here.


01:04:22.651 --> 01:04:25.863
- Hey, what's going on?
- Waiting for the all-clear.


01:04:25.946 --> 01:04:28.449
Can't let you in.
Could be a fire in there.


01:04:28.532 --> 01:04:30.451
I need to go inside.
My dog is in there.


01:04:30.534 --> 01:04:31.827
No can do.


01:04:35.080 --> 01:04:37.486
You said it yourself,
you've never been a


01:04:37.498 --> 01:04:40.210
pet. So you don't know
what that bond is like.


01:04:40.294 --> 01:04:42.212
I don't believe in that anymore.


01:04:42.296 --> 01:04:44.423
And maybe you'll
stop believing too.


01:04:44.506 --> 01:04:47.843
After yearning to be a pet day
after day and year after year,


01:04:47.926 --> 01:04:51.889
on an island where the only
humans are skeletal remains


01:04:51.972 --> 01:04:55.392
of long-dead explorers.


01:04:55.476 --> 01:04:56.602
Close up the crates.


01:04:56.685 --> 01:04:58.979
So we can bid a fond farewell


01:04:59.063 --> 01:05:03.734
to the failed cats
and dogs of Zone 867.


01:05:07.154 --> 01:05:10.199
Hey, I said don't go
in there, you rebels.


01:05:11.116 --> 01:05:12.868
Eh. They'll be fine.


01:05:12.951 --> 01:05:15.079
We've got company.


01:05:18.290 --> 01:05:19.458
That's Max.


01:05:19.541 --> 01:05:20.584
And Zoe.


01:05:22.544 --> 01:05:26.423
They tracked my GPS collar.
Max must've noticed I was gone.


01:05:26.507 --> 01:05:28.759
He still does care about me.


01:05:28.842 --> 01:05:29.885
Stop him, girls.


01:05:35.849 --> 01:05:37.267
- Rog!
- Roger.


01:05:37.351 --> 01:05:38.435
Roger!


01:05:39.186 --> 01:05:41.188
Humans are gonna save us.


01:05:41.271 --> 01:05:42.898
Mm.


01:05:42.981 --> 01:05:44.274
Get rid of the humans.


01:05:44.358 --> 01:05:47.236
Oh, I'll do better than that.


01:05:48.403 --> 01:05:51.532
I did some late-night research


01:05:51.615 --> 01:05:56.328
that revealed frequencies
impacting the human brain.


01:05:59.248 --> 01:06:00.749
Ow!


01:06:01.333 --> 01:06:02.835
Jeez. What is that?


01:06:06.255 --> 01:06:07.255
Ow!


01:06:11.802 --> 01:06:12.970
Mom.


01:06:15.639 --> 01:06:17.808
- Stop it.
- You're hurting them.


01:06:22.187 --> 01:06:23.272
Close up the crates.


01:06:27.901 --> 01:06:29.778
Well, my work here is done.


01:06:29.862 --> 01:06:32.739
So I'm gonna make
like a bulldog and flee.


01:06:32.823 --> 01:06:35.242
Flee. Get it? Flea?


01:06:36.827 --> 01:06:38.829
Anyway, you all
have a nice trip.


01:06:38.912 --> 01:06:42.958
Zeek, bring me my iron-dog suit.


01:06:56.013 --> 01:06:57.014
What now?


01:06:57.097 --> 01:06:59.600
No one hurts my human.


01:07:01.810 --> 01:07:03.604
Oh, my head. Ah.


01:07:03.687 --> 01:07:05.397
My head. Just need a minute.


01:07:09.860 --> 01:07:11.320
I'm with you, partner.


01:07:11.403 --> 01:07:14.406
If my Zoe is in trouble, I'd
run through a brick wall for her.


01:07:19.411 --> 01:07:21.580
Why couldn't you have
locked us in a paper sack?


01:07:21.663 --> 01:07:24.124
Didn't want you
to get a paper cut.


01:07:26.960 --> 01:07:30.005
Nobody hurts my friends' humans.


01:07:33.592 --> 01:07:36.094
- Thanks, big guy.
- Yeah, I got your back, kid.


01:07:36.178 --> 01:07:37.512
This is so annoying.


01:07:44.603 --> 01:07:46.647
You really care
about them that much?


01:07:46.730 --> 01:07:48.190
We would do anything for them.


01:07:48.273 --> 01:07:49.399
That's what pets do.


01:07:49.483 --> 01:07:51.693
Just like they would
do anything for us.


01:07:53.820 --> 01:07:54.905
Ow.


01:07:58.200 --> 01:07:59.200
Ow.


01:08:16.843 --> 01:08:18.387
Hello.


01:08:25.185 --> 01:08:27.437
Yeah. Okay.


01:08:29.940 --> 01:08:32.818
Uh, what is this
thing I'm feeling?


01:08:32.901 --> 01:08:35.988
It's so strange.


01:08:36.071 --> 01:08:40.117
It's called affection. It's what
people do for the pets they love.


01:08:40.200 --> 01:08:41.243
You're a cool bird.


01:08:41.326 --> 01:08:44.454
I'm... I'm enjoying it.


01:08:44.538 --> 01:08:46.790
Enough of this.


01:08:46.873 --> 01:08:48.792
Want me to turn up the frequency


01:08:48.875 --> 01:08:51.336
and get that clingy,
foolish putz off you?


01:08:51.420 --> 01:08:54.673
No, turn it off. Let them go.


01:08:54.756 --> 01:08:56.341
I'm a changed bird.


01:08:56.425 --> 01:08:59.094
I've seen the light at
the end of the cage.


01:08:59.177 --> 01:09:00.679
What?


01:09:00.762 --> 01:09:02.055
- What?
- By the way,


01:09:02.139 --> 01:09:06.018
animals talking, our
little secret, okay?


01:09:06.101 --> 01:09:08.562
I got you, Superbird.


01:09:10.397 --> 01:09:12.441
Superbird?


01:09:12.524 --> 01:09:16.570
I didn't study code
every night for two years


01:09:16.653 --> 01:09:19.489
to watch you go soft on me.


01:09:19.573 --> 01:09:21.533
That was not the plan.


01:09:21.616 --> 01:09:24.328
Yeah, well, you
didn't make the plan.


01:09:24.411 --> 01:09:25.996
I did.


01:09:26.079 --> 01:09:28.206
I have a new purpose now.


01:09:28.290 --> 01:09:31.835
Everyone should feel
the love of a human.


01:09:31.918 --> 01:09:34.296
You're not going anywhere.


01:09:41.636 --> 01:09:44.806
What are you doing? It's over.


01:09:44.890 --> 01:09:48.143
So hand me the phone and
get ready for your new family.


01:09:48.226 --> 01:09:50.187
I don't want a family.


01:09:50.270 --> 01:09:56.485
And I don't wanna be trapped in a
tiny space being force-fed crickets.


01:09:56.568 --> 01:09:58.487
Okay, what do you want?


01:09:58.570 --> 01:10:00.238
I want it all.


01:10:00.322 --> 01:10:03.742
Reptiles once ruled
the planet unopposed.


01:10:03.825 --> 01:10:10.082
We were here millions of years
before dogs, before cats, before anyone.


01:10:10.165 --> 01:10:11.833
Not before fish.


01:10:11.917 --> 01:10:13.585
Fish don't count.


01:10:13.668 --> 01:10:17.005
It's time my reptilian
brothers and I


01:10:17.089 --> 01:10:22.177
once again take our place
at the top of the food chain.


01:10:22.260 --> 01:10:26.390
The top? That would
mean that... Exactly.


01:10:26.473 --> 01:10:28.600
Zeek, I order you to stop.


01:10:28.683 --> 01:10:31.395
Bird frequency, anyone?


01:10:37.692 --> 01:10:39.194
I gotta do something.


01:10:39.277 --> 01:10:40.779
I gotta get to that phone.


01:10:40.862 --> 01:10:42.280
No. You won't make it.


01:10:42.364 --> 01:10:44.783
There's always a moment.


01:10:44.866 --> 01:10:47.577
And this is that moment.


01:10:47.661 --> 01:10:49.746
Cover me, partner.


01:10:49.830 --> 01:10:51.498
Did you just call me partner?


01:10:51.581 --> 01:10:53.083
I'm going for that phone.


01:10:58.213 --> 01:11:00.215
Now, that's a field agent.


01:11:04.511 --> 01:11:06.430
Okay, girls, ready to rumble?


01:11:07.722 --> 01:11:10.392
But first, cat nap.


01:11:16.773 --> 01:11:17.983
Tapping out.


01:11:18.066 --> 01:11:19.234
Told you I was a ninja.


01:11:19.317 --> 01:11:20.902
Want some more
of this, cream puff?


01:11:20.986 --> 01:11:22.696
No, not again.


01:11:22.779 --> 01:11:28.034
That's what I thought,
160 pounds of pure wuss...


01:11:31.997 --> 01:11:33.874
It's all mine now.


01:11:40.505 --> 01:11:42.466
No parachute!


01:11:43.967 --> 01:11:45.760
Whoa, whoa, whoa!


01:11:48.430 --> 01:11:50.515
Your shots better be up-to-date.


01:11:51.558 --> 01:11:54.561
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Whoa, okay, okay...


01:11:54.644 --> 01:11:56.897
How about that? I can fly.


01:11:56.980 --> 01:12:01.485
If you know what's good for
you, you'll bring me that phone.


01:12:05.739 --> 01:12:07.741
What are you doing?


01:12:09.784 --> 01:12:13.455
Cats and dogs and
humans, back to normal.


01:12:13.538 --> 01:12:15.957
No!


01:12:16.041 --> 01:12:18.835
All pain frequencies erased.


01:12:18.919 --> 01:12:22.005
Just disabled your
GPS microchip.


01:12:22.088 --> 01:12:24.466
Your owners won't
know what happened.


01:12:28.553 --> 01:12:29.471
Are you okay?


01:12:29.554 --> 01:12:30.764
Yeah. Are you?


01:12:30.847 --> 01:12:31.847
Yeah.


01:12:41.775 --> 01:12:43.193
What was that?


01:12:43.693 --> 01:12:45.445
Wait.


01:12:45.529 --> 01:12:49.157
Roger's GPS collar,
it's gone. Disappeared.


01:12:49.241 --> 01:12:51.535
So he's not inside?


01:12:51.618 --> 01:12:55.330
Stupid phone. Probably
didn't work in the first place.


01:12:55.413 --> 01:12:57.415
Did I tell you not
to go in there?


01:12:57.499 --> 01:13:00.460
- Should we head back to the house?
- Yeah.


01:13:00.544 --> 01:13:02.796
Just ignore me.


01:13:03.797 --> 01:13:05.715
There you are.


01:13:06.883 --> 01:13:10.345
- I saw the coolest bird.
- Oh, a bird?


01:13:10.428 --> 01:13:13.139
Dude, it's an emergency,
off your phone.


01:13:17.018 --> 01:13:19.813
All right, everyone,
sorry about that.


01:13:20.146 --> 01:13:22.357
Do with me what you want.


01:13:22.440 --> 01:13:24.317
This is not over.


01:13:24.401 --> 01:13:26.361
Oh, I think it is.


01:13:28.405 --> 01:13:29.906
Case closed, lizard.


01:13:29.990 --> 01:13:32.576
What? No!


01:13:32.659 --> 01:13:35.704
I think it's finally
time I retire.


01:13:35.787 --> 01:13:38.373
There's always a
moment. Right, old buddy?


01:13:39.165 --> 01:13:42.586
Wait. Your old partner,
your mentor, that was Ed?


01:13:42.669 --> 01:13:45.297
I always knew he
was a field agent.


01:13:45.380 --> 01:13:47.632
Just had to make sure he knew.


01:13:47.716 --> 01:13:52.262
Tell me something, Ed, did
you get captured on purpose?


01:13:52.345 --> 01:13:54.389
Just wanted a Drumstick.


01:13:54.472 --> 01:13:55.890
So, what about him?


01:13:55.974 --> 01:14:00.812
Like I said, we'll talk to headquarters,
see if they can help him find a home.


01:14:00.895 --> 01:14:02.480
And him?


01:14:04.357 --> 01:14:07.235
If you don't mind, I may
have a home for him too.


01:14:07.319 --> 01:14:10.405
Speaking of, we gotta get
home before Max and Zoe.


01:14:10.488 --> 01:14:12.157
How are we gonna do that?


01:14:12.240 --> 01:14:15.493
Oh, I got you. I
can help you there.


01:14:20.248 --> 01:14:22.375
Paws at 10 and 2.


01:14:27.297 --> 01:14:29.633
Uh-oh. Hit the brakes.


01:14:29.716 --> 01:14:31.468
Brakes! Brakes, brakes?


01:14:32.636 --> 01:14:33.636
I'm here.


01:14:33.678 --> 01:14:36.478
I think I need a full 20
hours of sleep tonight.


01:14:36.490 --> 01:14:38.683
I could go for a
long cat nap myself.


01:14:50.945 --> 01:14:53.114
Roger, what are
you doing in here?


01:14:53.198 --> 01:14:54.574
Gwen?


01:14:57.035 --> 01:14:59.329
That's a good boy, Roger.


01:14:59.412 --> 01:15:01.623
- How did he get in here?
- I don't know.


01:15:03.416 --> 01:15:04.501
Hey.


01:15:04.584 --> 01:15:07.253
Dad, uh, this is
Max from upstairs.


01:15:07.337 --> 01:15:09.464
- Hello.
- Sir.


01:15:09.547 --> 01:15:11.049
Hey.


01:15:11.132 --> 01:15:12.676
So...


01:15:13.968 --> 01:15:16.179
Anything exciting happen today?


01:15:17.389 --> 01:15:21.393
Um, actually, Dad, can you sit down?
There's something I wanna show you.


01:15:22.060 --> 01:15:23.645
Oh. Okay.


01:15:29.150 --> 01:15:33.238
I've been working on your song.
And this is what I came up with.


01:15:42.831 --> 01:15:45.291
♪ <i>Run, run, run</i> ♪


01:15:47.293 --> 01:15:49.587
♪ <i>Run, run, run</i> ♪


01:15:51.631 --> 01:15:53.591
♪ <i>Run, run, run</i> ♪


01:15:53.675 --> 01:15:54.801
Yeah.


01:15:56.052 --> 01:16:00.223
<i>Turns out, everyone found
exactly what they were looking for.</i>


01:16:00.306 --> 01:16:02.559
♪ <i>Didn't follow the plan</i> ♪


01:16:03.852 --> 01:16:07.522
♪ <i>I should've stopped
when I had the chance</i> ♪


01:16:07.605 --> 01:16:09.190
<i>Like a well-deserved rest.</i>


01:16:10.358 --> 01:16:11.901
<i>Like new-found confidence-</i>


01:16:11.985 --> 01:16:15.405
Zone 867, all clear
and looking good.


01:16:16.489 --> 01:16:18.366
<i>Like refocused priorities.</i>


01:16:18.450 --> 01:16:20.869
<i>Just chill.</i>


01:16:20.952 --> 01:16:23.663
Come on, Max. You got this.


01:16:23.747 --> 01:16:25.457
♪ <i>It's time we disconnect</i> ♪


01:16:26.040 --> 01:16:29.669
♪ <i>Run, run, run Our
minds are losing it ♪</i>


01:16:29.753 --> 01:16:31.296
♪ <i>Run, run, run</i> ♪


01:16:38.261 --> 01:16:39.554
That was amazing.


01:16:39.637 --> 01:16:41.806
That's my boy.


01:16:41.890 --> 01:16:43.057
Wow.


01:16:45.143 --> 01:16:46.603
State champion!


01:16:47.729 --> 01:16:49.314
You got your tennis mojo back.


01:16:49.397 --> 01:16:51.775
I just had to do it
on my own terms.


01:16:51.858 --> 01:16:53.985
All I had to do
was chill, chill...


01:16:54.068 --> 01:16:56.196
- And chill.
- Chill.


01:16:56.279 --> 01:16:57.614
<i>Like just letting go.</i>


01:16:57.697 --> 01:17:00.283
- I believe that's yours.
- Thank you.


01:17:00.366 --> 01:17:01.451
Good job.


01:17:01.534 --> 01:17:05.079
♪ <i>I never, never, never
